  "caption": "Quinn rolled an ankle on a rogue kerb, watched it puff up like a bread roll, then tried sitting perfectly still.\n\nSwelling is part of healing. It brings repair materials to the area. What tends to slow things down is fluid pooling, and moving muscles help pump it back up.\n\nWhat often helps: gentle movement like ankle pumps within comfort, elevating above heart level, a snug compression sleeve (loosen it if you notice tingling or colour change), and short bursts of ice for comfort so moving feels easier.\n\nA tight, tender calf, spreading redness or heat, fever, a joint that balloons quickly, numbness or swelling that keeps getting worse needs same-day medical care.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
